\description{
From a path of solutions that contains \eqn{\alpha = 1/2}, computes for each \eqn{\alpha \ge 1/2} the relative gain of contrast \eqn{\delta_V = \Delta V/V(u^\star_{1/2})}, the relative loss of squared level \eqn{\delta_{\bar a} = -\Delta\bar a^2/\bar a(u^\star_{1/2})^2}, and the interval \eqn{[(1-\alpha)/\alpha\,\rho\,\delta_{\bar a},\ \rho\,\delta_{\bar a}]} that contains \eqn{\delta_V} (corollary 2 of the article), with \eqn{\rho = \bar a^2/V} computed at INDORT. Since \eqn{\delta_{\bar a} \le 1}, \eqn{\rho} bounds a priori the relative gain of contrast that VOSA can bring.
}
